      "text": "Let $AE = CF = x$ and let $BD = d$.  Then\n\n\\begin{eqnarray*}d^{2} &=& AD^{2} + CD^{2} \\\\ &=& x^{2} + (1-x)^{2} \\\\ &=& x^{2} + 1 - 2x + x^{2} \\\\ &=& 2x^{2} - 2x + 1 \\\\ &=& d^{2} \\\\ \\end{eqnarray*}\n\nSo, $d = \\sqrt{2}x - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$, and $(\\sqrt{2}x - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})^{2} = x^{2} + (1-x)^{2}$.  Solving for $x$, we have:\n\n\\begin{eqnarray*}2x^{2} - \\sqrt{2}x + \\frac{1}{2} &=& x^{2} + 1 - 2x + x^{2} \\\\ \\iff & & x^{2} + 2x - \\frac{1}{2} = 0 \\\\ \\iff & & (x + 1)(x - \\frac{1}{2}) = 0 \\\\ \\end{eqnarray*}\n\nThe only real solution is $x = \\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nThe integer value of $k+m$ is $1+2 = \\boxed{3}$. The answer is: 3",
