      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let $D$ denote the lower right corner of the rectangle $AB\\vec{FDR}$, $H$ the intersection of $BD$ and $AE$, and $G$ the intersection of $BD$ and $CF$. Let $DF = FH$, $DE = ES$, and $MD = coth$. \n\nAt point $E$, using the Pythagorean Theorem, the vertical distance $HE$ can be calculated as:\n\\[HE = \\frac{AE}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{k} - m}{\\sqrt{2}}\\]\n\nBy the properties of a rectangular folding, points $D$, $E$, $F$, and $G$ are always collinear on line $\\overline{FG}$. At point $H$, the line segments $FD$ and $ED$ are perpendicular to $HJ$. This implies:\n\\[EH^{2} + HD^{2} = BD^{2}\\]\n\\[HF^{2} + HF^{2} = BD^{2}\\]\n\\[HD^{2} + DF^{2} = BD^{2}\\]\n\nSubstituting the known values:\n\\[\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{k} - m}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^{2} + \\left(\\frac{1 - m}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^{2} = 1^{2}\\]\n\\[\\left(\\sqrt{k} - m\\right)^{2} + \\left(1 - m\\right)^{2} = 2\\]\n\nExpanding and simplifying the equation:\n\\[k - 2m\\sqrt{k} + m^{2} + 1 - 2m + m^{2} = 2\\]\n\\[2m^{2} - 2m\\sqrt{k} + k - 1 = 0\\]\n\nBy applying the discriminant to the quadratic equation in $m$:\n\\[2m^{2} - 2m\\sqrt{k} + k - 1 = 0\\]\n\\[m_{diff}^{2} = (\\sqrt{k} \\pm \\sqrt{k^2 - 4(k - 1)})\\]\n\\[m_{diff} = \\frac{\\sqrt{k} \\pm \\sqrt{k^2 - 4(k - 1)}}{2}\\]\n\\[m_{diff} = \\frac{\\sqrt{k} \\pm \\sqrt{k - 4k + 4}}{2}\\]\n\\[m = \\frac{\\sqrt{k} \\pm \\sqrt{k - 3}}{2}\\]\n\nConsidering the positive root (as $m$ must be a rational number):\n\\[m = \\frac{\\sqrt{k} + \\sqrt{k - 3}}{2}\\]\n\nSubstituting $m$ back into the original expression for $AE$:\n\\[AE = \\sqrt{k} - m = \\sqrt{k} - \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{k} + \\sqrt{k - 3}}{2}\\right)\\]\n\\[AE = \\frac{2\\sqrt{k} - \\sqrt{k} - \\sqrt{k - 3}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{k} - \\sqrt{k - 3}}{2}\\]\n\nTo determine $k$ for which this expression holds, we solve:\n\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{k - 3}}{\\sqrt{k}} = \\frac{1}{2}\\]\n\\[\\frac{k - 3}{k} = \\frac{1}{4}\\]\n\\[4k - 12 = k\\]\n\\[3k = 12\\]\n\\[k = 4\\]\n\nTherefore, $AE = \\sqrt{4} - \\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{1}$.",
